{
  "$comment": "Shared fact conformance vectors (PR 4, #156). Every category is an array of { input, expected }. canonicalNumber: expected null means not a constant (canonicalNumber returns undefined); an integer result prints as plain digits, a result with |v| >= 2^53 is not a constant, and a non-zero result that rounds to 0 at 6 decimals is not a constant. isTrivialLiteral: a number literal is evaluated as in canonicalNumber and the double is compared exactly with the list's numbers (0.9999999 is not 1). hasRetryTimeoutFragment: tokens are ASCII only (A-Z, a-z, 0-9); every other character separates tokens; no Unicode case tests and no locale-dependent lowercasing. matchesNormalizationPattern: an absent qualifier means the call has no receiver (written Name(...)). Categories without a list in their input use the defaults block. normalizeFactText and capFactValue: input and expected are segment arrays, concatenated; a segment is a string or { repeat, count }. languageSpecific holds vectors only one language's copy runs: raw-string decoding is language-specific (csharp: C# raw string literals); Java text blocks get their own rule and vectors in PR 4.1 Task 6.",
  "defaults": {
    "trivialLiterals": [
      0,
      1,
      -1,
      null,
      true,
      false,
      ""
    ],
    "normalizationMethods": [
      "ToLower*",
      "ToUpper*",
      "Trim*",
      "Normalize",
      "toLowerCase",
      "toUpperCase",
      "trim",
      "strings.ToLower",
      "strings.TrimSpace",
      "equalsIgnoreCase"
    ]
  },
